msgid "HELP_TEXT"
msgstr "Tab is a map of the six guitar strings. The top line is string 1, the thinnest and highest-sounding string. A number tells you which fret to press; 0 means play the open string. The staff above is a pitch and rhythm reference: higher notes appear higher up. Guitar treble is written one octave above its sound. A measure is a small group of beats between vertical lines. The moving line follows the original timing; outlined notes show what is sounding. The reading key pairs note colors with open strings, first frets and hand moves; the fret number remains the instruction. The optional shape cues repeat those groups with a circle, triangle, or diamond in both staff and tab. A rest symbol means do not play. A ! or △ marks a note this arrangement could not place. Use From and Through to repeat a short section."

